{
  "audio_file": "demo_files/audioin_compressed.m4a",
  "audio_size_bytes": 10560193,
  "elapsed_ms": 48284,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 7.22,
      "end": 9.6,
      "text": "When you start a new software project,"
    },
    {
      "start": 9.8,
      "end": 12.7,
      "text": "you're super excited about the potential of"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.7,
      "end": 16.22,
      "text": "the project and you want to get moving as soon as possible,"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.0,
      "end": 20.06,
      "text": "which is great. Often when that project"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.38,
      "end": 23.88,
      "text": "matures and you get more customers and you get more users,"
    },
    {
      "start": 24.58,
      "end": 26.24,
      "text": "things need to change because you start"
    },
    {
      "start": 26.24,
      "end": 29.14,
      "text": "getting feedback from your customers. That's one thing."
    },
    {
      "start": 29.14,
      "end": 33.08,
      "text": "The other thing that happens is technologies change."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.66,
      "end": 34.74,
      "text": "Database systems might change."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.98,
      "end": 36.92,
      "text": "You might have to add a new user interface."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.32,
      "end": 40.92,
      "text": "You want to be able to do these things without"
    },
    {
      "start": 41.2,
      "end": 44.1,
      "text": "having to rewrite all of the logic."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.0,
      "end": 46.0,
      "text": "How do you do this?"
    },
    {
      "start": 46.76,
      "end": 50.7,
      "text": "I've been running software companies for the past 30 years."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.0,
      "end": 55.3,
      "text": "At some point, I was, what's the word,"
    },
    {
      "start": 55.56,
      "end": 58.38,
      "text": "dismayed or surprised to see how difficult it"
    },
    {
      "start": 58.38,
      "end": 62.98,
      "text": "becomes to change things if the logic is all over the place."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.76,
      "end": 66.54,
      "text": "If you have business logic in your database layer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 66.88,
      "end": 68.28,
      "text": "in your business logic layer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 68.46,
      "end": 70.44,
      "text": "sometimes in your user interface layer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 70.86,
      "end": 73.48,
      "text": "little rules that you've got everywhere,"
    },
    {
      "start": 74.42,
      "end": 76.26,
      "text": "then at some point,"
    },
    {
      "start": 76.38,
      "end": 78.74,
      "text": "nobody knows really what all these rules are."
    },
    {
      "start": 79.08,
      "end": 80.14,
      "text": "This is what happens."
    },
    {
      "start": 80.68,
      "end": 82.62,
      "text": "As you're moving really quickly in the beginning,"
    },
    {
      "start": 82.8,
      "end": 85.38,
      "text": "somebody asks for a feature and one of"
    },
    {
      "start": 85.38,
      "end": 87.54,
      "text": "the developers goes and just adds it somewhere."
    },
    {
      "start": 87.54,
      "end": 91.34,
      "text": "If there's no real clear rule where that should be,"
    },
    {
      "start": 92.78,
      "end": 93.82,
      "text": "that could be in the front end,"
    },
    {
      "start": 94.0,
      "end": 97.16,
      "text": "it should be in some form of business logic layer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 97.2,
      "end": 98.12,
      "text": "it could be in the database,"
    },
    {
      "start": 98.36,
      "end": 100.2,
      "text": "it could be a stored procedure or a view"
    },
    {
      "start": 100.2,
      "end": 102.16,
      "text": "or something that contains that logic."
    },
    {
      "start": 102.8,
      "end": 107.74,
      "text": "If this keeps on happening over a few years for a very successful project,"
    },
    {
      "start": 108.0,
      "end": 112.02,
      "text": "you are stuck because you won't have the time to go"
    },
    {
      "start": 112.02,
      "end": 114.26,
      "text": "back and understand what exactly"
    },
    {
      "start": 114.26,
      "end": 117.16,
      "text": "are all these little rules that was implemented."
    },
    {
      "start": 117.16,
      "end": 122.02,
      "text": "Some of them are micro rules that affect big things"
    },
    {
      "start": 122.02,
      "end": 126.32,
      "text": "like the way interest is calculated or the way finances are created."
    },
    {
      "start": 127.14,
      "end": 131.06,
      "text": "That's the problem that layers solve."
    },
    {
      "start": 131.74,
      "end": 134.78,
      "text": "Layered architecture, specifically what"
    },
    {
      "start": 134.78,
      "end": 136.56,
      "text": "we're going to talk about now is clean architecture."
    },
    {
      "start": 136.92,
      "end": 139.34,
      "text": "This is the problem that it solves and I'm going to"
    },
    {
      "start": 139.34,
      "end": 141.48,
      "text": "talk about this right now really quickly."
    },
    {
      "start": 142.36,
      "end": 150.16,
      "text": "In Episode 3, the mission here that we need to do is we"
    },
    {
      "start": 150.16,
      "end": 154.5,
      "text": "need to refactor our code into these different layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 155.3,
      "end": 157.78,
      "text": "We need to implement a rule,"
    },
    {
      "start": 158.04,
      "end": 160.18,
      "text": "that's the dependency rule in clean architecture,"
    },
    {
      "start": 160.38,
      "end": 163.26,
      "text": "that mean that all dependencies point inwards."
    },
    {
      "start": 163.48,
      "end": 165.18,
      "text": "Let's talk about this."
    },
    {
      "start": 166.68,
      "end": 169.28,
      "text": "You need to go to Episode 2, clone this code."
    },
    {
      "start": 169.34,
      "end": 170.42,
      "text": "This is the code you'll use."
    },
    {
      "start": 170.42,
      "end": 172.88,
      "text": "Look at ReadQuest 3."
    },
    {
      "start": 173.04,
      "end": 174.7,
      "text": "This is the instruction for Quest 3."
    },
    {
      "start": 175.44,
      "end": 176.18,
      "text": "Read through all of this,"
    },
    {
      "start": 176.36,
      "end": 178.74,
      "text": "read the blog there by Robert C. Martin."
    },
    {
      "start": 179.3,
      "end": 180.74,
      "text": "The blog's a bit dated,"
    },
    {
      "start": 180.84,
      "end": 182.6,
      "text": "some of the terminology is a bit old."
    },
    {
      "start": 182.86,
      "end": 185.72,
      "text": "I'm going to talk through some of these concepts right now."
    },
    {
      "start": 186.48,
      "end": 189.9,
      "text": "Then we need to refactor to the delivery layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 190.16,
      "end": 191.72,
      "text": "You'll see the different layers over here."
    },
    {
      "start": 192.44,
      "end": 195.06,
      "text": "Just go back. The application layer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 195.44,
      "end": 197.36,
      "text": "the domain layer, and the infrastructure layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 197.36,
      "end": 200.52,
      "text": "At this point, we're going to implement these four layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 202.16,
      "end": 205.88,
      "text": "You could, sometimes the layers are called something different."
    },
    {
      "start": 206.02,
      "end": 209.04,
      "text": "Some people call it presentation layer instead of delivery layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 209.58,
      "end": 210.64,
      "text": "Some have more layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 211.22,
      "end": 214.08,
      "text": "This will be a great overview of how this works."
    },
    {
      "start": 214.14,
      "end": 215.58,
      "text": "Let's keep it simple like this."
    },
    {
      "start": 215.62,
      "end": 217.5,
      "text": "I love these wording,"
    },
    {
      "start": 217.62,
      "end": 219.7,
      "text": "specifically delivery layer because that's where"
    },
    {
      "start": 219.7,
      "end": 222.1,
      "text": "your application is delivered to the world."
    },
    {
      "start": 222.16,
      "end": 224.36,
      "text": "It's also responsible for"
    },
    {
      "start": 224.36,
      "end": 228.1,
      "text": "delivering incoming messages to the application itself."
    },
    {
      "start": 229.54,
      "end": 231.8,
      "text": "Then we'll enforce the dependency rule."
    },
    {
      "start": 231.86,
      "end": 233.22,
      "text": "This is going to be a big one,"
    },
    {
      "start": 233.38,
      "end": 236.8,
      "text": "and there's an interesting code that you need to write to get this done."
    },
    {
      "start": 237.92,
      "end": 241.12,
      "text": "That's more of a visual overview of the dependencies."
    },
    {
      "start": 242.74,
      "end": 245.56,
      "text": "Then what I also did is I showed you what"
    },
    {
      "start": 245.56,
      "end": 249.16,
      "text": "the project structure should look like once you're done."
    },
    {
      "start": 250.3,
      "end": 252.26,
      "text": "This is what you're seeing right here."
    },
    {
      "start": 252.26,
      "end": 255.02,
      "text": "Success criteria code is organized into layers,"
    },
    {
      "start": 256.44,
      "end": 257.5,
      "text": "which is folders."
    },
    {
      "start": 257.84,
      "end": 260.8,
      "text": "These are folders described above."
    },
    {
      "start": 261.1,
      "end": 263.94,
      "text": "Inner layers do not reference names from the outer layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 264.12,
      "end": 265.64,
      "text": "That is the dependency rule."
    },
    {
      "start": 266.08,
      "end": 269.3,
      "text": "Any broken dependencies are fixed after the move."
    },
    {
      "start": 270.3,
      "end": 272.62,
      "text": "You just add a docs folder as well."
    },
    {
      "start": 273.26,
      "end": 275.24,
      "text": "That's just a typical standard."
    },
    {
      "start": 276.12,
      "end": 278.26,
      "text": "I'm going to talk you through this."
    },
    {
      "start": 278.36,
      "end": 279.32,
      "text": "What is this all about?"
    },
    {
      "start": 279.46,
      "end": 281.56,
      "text": "Keep the most important logic separate."
    },
    {
      "start": 281.56,
      "end": 284.02,
      "text": "I talked earlier about business logic."
    },
    {
      "start": 284.18,
      "end": 287.32,
      "text": "We want to keep that into the domain and application layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 287.86,
      "end": 291.1,
      "text": "Those are the two layers that need to know about business logic."
    },
    {
      "start": 291.98,
      "end": 295.08,
      "text": "The other layers have infrastructure as well as"
    },
    {
      "start": 295.08,
      "end": 299.26,
      "text": "the delivery mechanisms like the fast API or command line interface."
    },
    {
      "start": 299.72,
      "end": 305.02,
      "text": "We'll talk about that now. Problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 305.12,
      "end": 306.7,
      "text": "when everything is slightly connected,"
    },
    {
      "start": 306.88,
      "end": 307.8,
      "text": "changes get harder."
    },
    {
      "start": 308.24,
      "end": 309.54,
      "text": "That's what I talked about earlier."
    },
    {
      "start": 310.06,
      "end": 311.84,
      "text": "Bugs spread farther."
    },
    {
      "start": 312.36,
      "end": 314.7,
      "text": "Things are connected all over the place,"
    },
    {
      "start": 315.52,
      "end": 316.88,
      "text": "and one thing affects another thing,"
    },
    {
      "start": 317.2,
      "end": 320.94,
      "text": "and when one thing breaks, everything breaks."
    },
    {
      "start": 322.44,
      "end": 324.76,
      "text": "That's the bugs spread farther concept."
    },
    {
      "start": 325.2,
      "end": 328.68,
      "text": "Testing becomes painful because now you need to test everything."
    },
    {
      "start": 328.88,
      "end": 329.96,
      "text": "You need to test your database,"
    },
    {
      "start": 330.26,
      "end": 331.94,
      "text": "your front end, your business logic."
    },
    {
      "start": 332.04,
      "end": 333.52,
      "text": "All of this are intertwined."
    },
    {
      "start": 333.98,
      "end": 334.96,
      "text": "In a clean architecture,"
    },
    {
      "start": 335.14,
      "end": 337.84,
      "text": "you can test only your domain and application."
    },
    {
      "start": 337.84,
      "end": 339.68,
      "text": "You can test only your domain logic,"
    },
    {
      "start": 339.84,
      "end": 341.94,
      "text": "and then you can also test your application,"
    },
    {
      "start": 343.06,
      "end": 344.28,
      "text": "use cases, and services."
    },
    {
      "start": 344.82,
      "end": 347.36,
      "text": "Then you can go and test infrastructure as well,"
    },
    {
      "start": 347.44,
      "end": 349.22,
      "text": "but those are the hearts of it,"
    },
    {
      "start": 349.22,
      "end": 351.48,
      "text": "and you can keep those tests separate,"
    },
    {
      "start": 352.22,
      "end": 354.9,
      "text": "which ends up surprisingly making the test"
    },
    {
      "start": 354.94,
      "end": 357.3,
      "text": "sometimes hundreds of times faster to do."
    },
    {
      "start": 357.56,
      "end": 360.94,
      "text": "You can run hundreds of tests within less than a second,"
    },
    {
      "start": 361.06,
      "end": 363.42,
      "text": "versus if you need to involve databases,"
    },
    {
      "start": 364.14,
      "end": 366.56,
      "text": "it becomes substantially slower."
    },
    {
      "start": 366.56,
      "end": 369.72,
      "text": "We can do these tests in memory,"
    },
    {
      "start": 370.3,
      "end": 371.54,
      "text": "and we're going to talk about that"
    },
    {
      "start": 371.54,
      "end": 376.28,
      "text": "when we look at the repository pattern and the unit of work."
    },
    {
      "start": 376.6,
      "end": 378.06,
      "text": "Testing becomes painful,"
    },
    {
      "start": 378.18,
      "end": 381.26,
      "text": "new features becomes riskier because now you're changing stuff,"
    },
    {
      "start": 381.3,
      "end": 384.02,
      "text": "and it can break stuff in unexpected ways."
    },
    {
      "start": 384.5,
      "end": 386.32,
      "text": "Mental models become more complex."
    },
    {
      "start": 386.42,
      "end": 389.12,
      "text": "This is the thing that I really have found."
    },
    {
      "start": 389.26,
      "end": 390.4,
      "text": "If you have a clean architecture,"
    },
    {
      "start": 390.54,
      "end": 392.02,
      "text": "you have this folder structure,"
    },
    {
      "start": 392.5,
      "end": 396.04,
      "text": "and you have the concept of dependencies only pointing inwards,"
    },
    {
      "start": 396.04,
      "end": 399.34,
      "text": "then you have a clear understanding of how everything works,"
    },
    {
      "start": 400.02,
      "end": 401.7,
      "text": "which is really important."
    },
    {
      "start": 402.2,
      "end": 403.46,
      "text": "Computers don't struggle with this,"
    },
    {
      "start": 403.52,
      "end": 405.54,
      "text": "but software developers do,"
    },
    {
      "start": 405.84,
      "end": 408.72,
      "text": "and I feel especially now in the world of AI"
    },
    {
      "start": 408.72,
      "end": 413.9,
      "text": "where code can get generated in its millions of lines in minutes,"
    },
    {
      "start": 414.62,
      "end": 418.62,
      "text": "it's really important to keep the structure well-organized,"
    },
    {
      "start": 418.96,
      "end": 422.02,
      "text": "keep the dependencies well-understood,"
    },
    {
      "start": 422.66,
      "end": 426.2,
      "text": "have a mental model which you can participate on"
    },
    {
      "start": 426.2,
      "end": 427.96,
      "text": "instead of just being an observer"
    },
    {
      "start": 427.96,
      "end": 430.22,
      "text": "and trying to figure out what AI is doing."
    },
    {
      "start": 430.5,
      "end": 433.14,
      "text": "That will be a recipe for a disaster."
    },
    {
      "start": 434.04,
      "end": 437.06,
      "text": "So I feel it's even more important now to have this."
    },
    {
      "start": 437.36,
      "end": 440.76,
      "text": "Business rules end up locked to specific tools."
    },
    {
      "start": 441.02,
      "end": 442.72,
      "text": "That's part of the..."
    },
    {
      "start": 442.72,
      "end": 445.64,
      "text": "You, for example, have business logic in FastAPI."
    },
    {
      "start": 445.88,
      "end": 448.66,
      "text": "It's a disaster because then if you have a command line interface,"
    },
    {
      "start": 448.76,
      "end": 449.96,
      "text": "you need to repeat it there."
    },
    {
      "start": 449.96,
      "end": 452.58,
      "text": "If you have events coming in, you need to repeat it,"
    },
    {
      "start": 452.74,
      "end": 455.3,
      "text": "and you end up repeating yourself all the time."
    },
    {
      "start": 456.1,
      "end": 458.94,
      "text": "The simple solution, put core business rules in the center,"
    },
    {
      "start": 459.2,
      "end": 461.3,
      "text": "put changing technology on the outside."
    },
    {
      "start": 461.7,
      "end": 464.06,
      "text": "FastAPI is an example, or a command line interface,"
    },
    {
      "start": 464.66,
      "end": 467.7,
      "text": "or databases, or messaging infrastructure,"
    },
    {
      "start": 468.18,
      "end": 469.68,
      "text": "or authenticating systems."
    },
    {
      "start": 470.16,
      "end": 472.88,
      "text": "Keep the center stable even if the outside changes."
    },
    {
      "start": 473.14,
      "end": 475.16,
      "text": "Do not couple parts together unnecessarily."
    },
    {
      "start": 475.76,
      "end": 478.28,
      "text": "This is a visual overview of the layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 478.64,
      "end": 481.72,
      "text": "Delivery on the outside, dependencies pointing inwards,"
    },
    {
      "start": 482.34,
      "end": 485.46,
      "text": "infrastructure, application, domain is the heart of the system."
    },
    {
      "start": 486.22,
      "end": 491.16,
      "text": "The application layer is like an API that works with the domain."
    },
    {
      "start": 491.32,
      "end": 493.2,
      "text": "So they go hand in hand."
    },
    {
      "start": 496.66,
      "end": 499.58,
      "text": "This is... I just put these on here so you can see."
    },
    {
      "start": 499.64,
      "end": 501.02,
      "text": "When we're talking about the outer layer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 501.18,
      "end": 503.86,
      "text": "command line interfaces, web APIs, user interfaces,"
    },
    {
      "start": 503.86,
      "end": 506.42,
      "text": "incoming events, GraphQL API script,"
    },
    {
      "start": 506.94,
      "end": 508.96,
      "text": "those are the entry points."
    },
    {
      "start": 509.36,
      "end": 512.82,
      "text": "That's where you deliver your application logic to."
    },
    {
      "start": 514.2,
      "end": 517.04,
      "text": "Also, anything coming in from a script, as an example,"
    },
    {
      "start": 517.16,
      "end": 520.72,
      "text": "or an event that gets delivered to the inner parts"
    },
    {
      "start": 520.72,
      "end": 522.72,
      "text": "of your application from the delivery layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 523.16,
      "end": 525.72,
      "text": "Again, that's why I like the terminology delivery layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 526.84,
      "end": 529.54,
      "text": "Infrastructure layer is where you put any infrastructure"
    },
    {
      "start": 529.54,
      "end": 531.8,
      "text": "that your application relies on."
    },
    {
      "start": 531.8,
      "end": 537.52,
      "text": "For example, database, file storage, messaging, external APIs."
    },
    {
      "start": 537.76,
      "end": 541.2,
      "text": "You might have a Twilio integration or a payment solution integration."
    },
    {
      "start": 541.48,
      "end": 543.28,
      "text": "That will be in the infrastructure layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 543.58,
      "end": 544.38,
      "text": "Logging authentication."
    },
    {
      "start": 544.92,
      "end": 546.32,
      "text": "Then you have the application layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 546.52,
      "end": 548.74,
      "text": "That's where you define your data transfer objects."
    },
    {
      "start": 549.26,
      "end": 551.44,
      "text": "We're going to talk about that in the next episode."
    },
    {
      "start": 552.68,
      "end": 556.2,
      "text": "These could be dictionaries or classes objects"
    },
    {
      "start": 556.2,
      "end": 560.06,
      "text": "that get sent from the delivery layer into the application layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 561.18,
      "end": 565.42,
      "text": "Application services have use cases and those interact with"
    },
    {
      "start": 565.42,
      "end": 568.52,
      "text": "and use the domain layer and also interact with the infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "start": 569.12,
      "end": 573.22,
      "text": "Then you have the heart of the system, the pure rules."
    },
    {
      "start": 573.72,
      "end": 575.44,
      "text": "These are, this is the domain layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 576.4,
      "end": 583.0,
      "text": "So, what, back in the day, 20 years ago,"
    },
    {
      "start": 583.92,
      "end": 587.32,
      "text": "before that, code was just all in a bunch of files,"
    },
    {
      "start": 587.56,
      "end": 588.72,
      "text": "similar to episode two."
    },
    {
      "start": 588.72,
      "end": 590.7,
      "text": "When we wrapped up episode two,"
    },
    {
      "start": 590.92,
      "end": 593.72,
      "text": "you had all of your code files in one big folder there."
    },
    {
      "start": 594.54,
      "end": 595.7,
      "text": "That's the way it used to be."
    },
    {
      "start": 597.48,
      "end": 601.26,
      "text": "But at least we separated them into some logical files."
    },
    {
      "start": 603.14,
      "end": 605.62,
      "text": "Steps back and it would be one big file of code."
    },
    {
      "start": 606.78,
      "end": 610.98,
      "text": "So, then people introduced a three-layered architecture"
    },
    {
      "start": 610.98,
      "end": 613.06,
      "text": "or sometimes four-layered architecture."
    },
    {
      "start": 613.6,
      "end": 616.76,
      "text": "That would be you're keeping your logic separate."
    },
    {
      "start": 616.76,
      "end": 618.24,
      "text": "You have your presentation layer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 618.72,
      "end": 620.24,
      "text": "and then you have a business logic layer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 620.64,
      "end": 622.18,
      "text": "and then you have the data access layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 623.22,
      "end": 625.9,
      "text": "Notice that the bottom layer here is the database"
    },
    {
      "start": 625.9,
      "end": 628.32,
      "text": "and everything depends on the database,"
    },
    {
      "start": 628.9,
      "end": 631.94,
      "text": "which is the exact opposite of what I just showed you."
    },
    {
      "start": 632.58,
      "end": 636.72,
      "text": "I want to compare clean architecture now to three-layered architecture"
    },
    {
      "start": 638.68,
      "end": 640.64,
      "text": "or three-tiered architecture."
    },
    {
      "start": 641.08,
      "end": 643.2,
      "text": "Clean architecture, you are,"
    },
    {
      "start": 643.2,
      "end": 647.0,
      "text": "your primary goal is decoupling logic from technology."
    },
    {
      "start": 648.32,
      "end": 650.84,
      "text": "Now, in three-tiered architecture, that's not the goal"
    },
    {
      "start": 650.84,
      "end": 653.16,
      "text": "because everything is coupled to the database."
    },
    {
      "start": 653.92,
      "end": 656.86,
      "text": "So, you're basically separating the tiers"
    },
    {
      "start": 657.42,
      "end": 661.38,
      "text": "into logical responsibilities or functional responsibilities."
    },
    {
      "start": 661.9,
      "end": 665.88,
      "text": "The center of the architecture in clean architecture is the domain."
    },
    {
      "start": 666.3,
      "end": 668.28,
      "text": "That's the heart of the business rules."
    },
    {
      "start": 668.78,
      "end": 672.46,
      "text": "And this was, what was his name?"
    },
    {
      "start": 673.06,
      "end": 676.98,
      "text": "So, Robert C. Martin expanded on this in his book, Clean Architecture,"
    },
    {
      "start": 677.76,
      "end": 681.26,
      "text": "but the original book was Domain-Driven Design."
    },
    {
      "start": 682.56,
      "end": 686.08,
      "text": "Domain-Driven Design clarified this idea"
    },
    {
      "start": 686.08,
      "end": 688.12,
      "text": "that if you keep your domain simple,"
    },
    {
      "start": 688.52,
      "end": 692.3,
      "text": "it becomes easy to understand what the application does."
    },
    {
      "start": 692.66,
      "end": 695.0,
      "text": "Everything else becomes a technical concern."
    },
    {
      "start": 695.5,
      "end": 699.18,
      "text": "But if you want to understand what the business logic is,"
    },
    {
      "start": 699.18,
      "end": 702.68,
      "text": "you'll look at your domain and then you'll go one step further."
    },
    {
      "start": 702.88,
      "end": 704.26,
      "text": "You'll look at your application layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 704.8,
      "end": 706.22,
      "text": "And combining those two,"
    },
    {
      "start": 706.36,
      "end": 709.18,
      "text": "you will have all of your business logic right there"
    },
    {
      "start": 709.18,
      "end": 711.34,
      "text": "and anything else will sit on the outside."
    },
    {
      "start": 711.86,
      "end": 715.56,
      "text": "And it's not messing around with your mental model"
    },
    {
      "start": 715.56,
      "end": 717.3,
      "text": "of understanding what this should do."
    },
    {
      "start": 718.32,
      "end": 720.68,
      "text": "So, whereas with a three-tiered architecture,"
    },
    {
      "start": 720.8,
      "end": 724.7,
      "text": "you have the database at the center, the schema at the center."
    },
    {
      "start": 725.12,
      "end": 728.5,
      "text": "Flexibility, clean architecture is highly flexible."
    },
    {
      "start": 728.5,
      "end": 731.3,
      "text": "You can swap a SQL database, no SQL."
    },
    {
      "start": 732.42,
      "end": 734.2,
      "text": "People always talk about swapping."
    },
    {
      "start": 734.82,
      "end": 737.72,
      "text": "Now, it doesn't happen often that you want to swap the database."
    },
    {
      "start": 738.52,
      "end": 740.9,
      "text": "So, I don't like that as an example."
    },
    {
      "start": 741.98,
      "end": 744.28,
      "text": "One of the biggest benefits that you do get"
    },
    {
      "start": 744.28,
      "end": 748.58,
      "text": "is all these other little technologies like FastAPI can be changed."
    },
    {
      "start": 749.34,
      "end": 754.26,
      "text": "In a clean architecture, you would be able to take a FastAPI"
    },
    {
      "start": 754.26,
      "end": 757.26,
      "text": "and change that to the next big thing."
    },
    {
      "start": 757.26,
      "end": 759.92,
      "text": "Only a few years ago, it was Flask."
    },
    {
      "start": 760.8,
      "end": 763.44,
      "text": "And you would be able to change Flask to FastAPI"
    },
    {
      "start": 764.22,
      "end": 766.1,
      "text": "without changing any other layer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 766.96,
      "end": 768.86,
      "text": "without touching any other layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 769.08,
      "end": 770.72,
      "text": "You'll only touch the delivery layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 772.52,
      "end": 774.88,
      "text": "You'll add a new command line interface"
    },
    {
      "start": 774.88,
      "end": 778.66,
      "text": "or you will adopt instead of a certain messaging system,"
    },
    {
      "start": 779.0,
      "end": 782.0,
      "text": "start using gRPC without touching any other layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 782.32,
      "end": 784.74,
      "text": "That's where the flexibility really comes in."
    },
    {
      "start": 784.86,
      "end": 786.24,
      "text": "That's the one big advantage."
    },
    {
      "start": 786.24,
      "end": 788.7,
      "text": "The other thing is the mental model,"
    },
    {
      "start": 789.18,
      "end": 792.56,
      "text": "the simplicity to understand what's going on in all of these layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 793.04,
      "end": 796.48,
      "text": "In a three-tiered architecture, the flexibility is moderate."
    },
    {
      "start": 796.92,
      "end": 800.04,
      "text": "Changing the database often requires rewriting parts of the business logic."
    },
    {
      "start": 800.28,
      "end": 802.38,
      "text": "Again, I don't want to focus on the database here."
    },
    {
      "start": 803.12,
      "end": 805.7,
      "text": "I want to show you something though."
    },
    {
      "start": 805.74,
      "end": 811.02,
      "text": "If you look at this, the arrows there are not talking about dependencies."
    },
    {
      "start": 812.66,
      "end": 814.84,
      "text": "The dependencies in a three-tiered architecture"
    },
    {
      "start": 814.84,
      "end": 816.7,
      "text": "often are all over the place."
    },
    {
      "start": 817.6,
      "end": 819.76,
      "text": "It's not such a big thing to say that,"
    },
    {
      "start": 820.06,
      "end": 823.68,
      "text": "oh, you need to, nothing needs to depend on something else."
    },
    {
      "start": 824.34,
      "end": 827.16,
      "text": "And that often becomes very messy."
    },
    {
      "start": 827.28,
      "end": 830.64,
      "text": "Whereas with clean architecture, you have an unbreakable rule,"
    },
    {
      "start": 831.48,
      "end": 835.46,
      "text": "the dependency rule, where everything points inwards."
    },
    {
      "start": 835.7,
      "end": 837.54,
      "text": "So I'm just bringing this up again."
    },
    {
      "start": 837.68,
      "end": 841.72,
      "text": "And then for a more clear view of the dependency rule,"
    },
    {
      "start": 841.86,
      "end": 842.68,
      "text": "look at this graph."
    },
    {
      "start": 842.68,
      "end": 847.54,
      "text": "It's often misunderstood that you have to go through all the layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 847.82,
      "end": 848.52,
      "text": "It's not the case."
    },
    {
      "start": 849.16,
      "end": 852.22,
      "text": "The delivery layer can talk directly to any other layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 853.08,
      "end": 856.76,
      "text": "The only thing is, the delivery layer knows about all layers"
    },
    {
      "start": 856.76,
      "end": 858.08,
      "text": "because it's the outside."
    },
    {
      "start": 858.68,
      "end": 861.54,
      "text": "But the moment you move one layer into the infrastructure layer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 861.68,
      "end": 864.78,
      "text": "it should not know anything about the delivery layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 864.94,
      "end": 867.56,
      "text": "So you should not even mention FastAPI there."
    },
    {
      "start": 867.84,
      "end": 870.94,
      "text": "This does become challenging from a programming point of view"
    },
    {
      "start": 870.94,
      "end": 875.98,
      "text": "when you use this concept of programming against interfaces"
    },
    {
      "start": 875.98,
      "end": 877.66,
      "text": "instead of implementations,"
    },
    {
      "start": 877.9,
      "end": 881.8,
      "text": "which we're going to look at in this episode as well,"
    },
    {
      "start": 881.88,
      "end": 884.86,
      "text": "because it affects us with the repository."
    },
    {
      "start": 885.28,
      "end": 887.5,
      "text": "If you look at episode two's code,"
    },
    {
      "start": 887.54,
      "end": 889.86,
      "text": "you'll see that the repository is mentioned"
    },
    {
      "start": 890.08,
      "end": 894.28,
      "text": "and imported into the application layer, which is wrong."
    },
    {
      "start": 894.84,
      "end": 897.92,
      "text": "Big challenge for you is going to be, how do you solve that?"
    },
    {
      "start": 898.52,
      "end": 902.38,
      "text": "How do you still keep a structure in the application layer"
    },
    {
      "start": 902.38,
      "end": 903.82,
      "text": "without mentioning JSON?"
    },
    {
      "start": 905.82,
      "end": 908.02,
      "text": "Application layer should not know about JSON."
    },
    {
      "start": 908.66,
      "end": 913.1,
      "text": "You should be able to swap JSON to, let's say, Postgres"
    },
    {
      "start": 913.1,
      "end": 915.04,
      "text": "without touching the application layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 916.42,
      "end": 920.36,
      "text": "Or JSON to Firebase without touching the..."
    },
    {
      "start": 920.36,
      "end": 922.84,
      "text": "You should even be able to support multiples."
    },
    {
      "start": 923.38,
      "end": 925.22,
      "text": "And often we see this with testing."
    },
    {
      "start": 925.22,
      "end": 926.86,
      "text": "Once you start testing the application,"
    },
    {
      "start": 927.26,
      "end": 928.86,
      "text": "you won't test it with JSON,"
    },
    {
      "start": 929.06,
      "end": 932.28,
      "text": "you'll test it with an in-memory memory store"
    },
    {
      "start": 932.34,
      "end": 936.26,
      "text": "to get that sub-second speed for all of your tests."
    },
    {
      "start": 936.4,
      "end": 938.5,
      "text": "If you run 100 tests, 200, 300 tests,"
    },
    {
      "start": 938.54,
      "end": 941.64,
      "text": "you want that to execute in seconds, not minutes."
    },
    {
      "start": 942.5,
      "end": 948.5,
      "text": "And that's going to be part of what we'll see how to do in this episode."
    },
    {
      "start": 950.92,
      "end": 953.52,
      "text": "So the layers, those are the layers I talked about."
    },
    {
      "start": 954.72,
      "end": 955.32,
      "text": "Domain."
    },
    {
      "start": 957.52,
      "end": 962.14,
      "text": "I've mentioned the domain, application layer, data transfer objects."
    },
    {
      "start": 963.02,
      "end": 964.38,
      "text": "We use Pydantic for that."
    },
    {
      "start": 964.5,
      "end": 966.48,
      "text": "We've already touched on that in episode one and two."
    },
    {
      "start": 967.48,
      "end": 971.76,
      "text": "Now, the data transfer objects transfer data from the delivery layer"
    },
    {
      "start": 971.76,
      "end": 974.72,
      "text": "to the application layer or other layers in a standard way."
    },
    {
      "start": 974.64,
      "end": 977.68,
      "text": "Typically, application layer, where we unpack it"
    },
    {
      "start": 977.68,
      "end": 980.14,
      "text": "and we start going through the use cases."
    },
    {
      "start": 983.46,
      "end": 984.06,
      "text": "Infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "start": 985.0,
      "end": 987.58,
      "text": "The main rule, inner parts should not depend on outer parts."
    },
    {
      "start": 987.68,
      "end": 988.52,
      "text": "We talked about that."
    },
    {
      "start": 989.08,
      "end": 992.7,
      "text": "The core should not know about the infrastructure or delivery details."
    },
    {
      "start": 993.14,
      "end": 995.3,
      "text": "Dependencies should point inwards."
    },
    {
      "start": 999.1,
      "end": 1000.22,
      "text": "Why this helps?"
    },
    {
      "start": 1001.52,
      "end": 1003.34,
      "text": "Anything we do has to have a reason."
    },
    {
      "start": 1004.24,
      "end": 1005.66,
      "text": "Easier to test the core logic."
    },
    {
      "start": 1005.92,
      "end": 1006.7,
      "text": "We talked about that."
    },
    {
      "start": 1006.96,
      "end": 1008.24,
      "text": "Tests become super fast."
    },
    {
      "start": 1008.62,
      "end": 1010.12,
      "text": "They also become isolated."
    },
    {
      "start": 1010.12,
      "end": 1014.8,
      "text": "You can test the domain on its own, then application use cases on its own"
    },
    {
      "start": 1014.8,
      "end": 1016.62,
      "text": "without even touching technology."
    },
    {
      "start": 1017.8,
      "end": 1022.82,
      "text": "The advantages are simpler tests as well as super fast tests."
    },
    {
      "start": 1024.12,
      "end": 1025.52,
      "text": "Easier to change tools later."
    },
    {
      "start": 1025.72,
      "end": 1027.46,
      "text": "You can swap out. We talked about that."
    },
    {
      "start": 1027.76,
      "end": 1029.18,
      "text": "Easier to understand the system."
    },
    {
      "start": 1029.46,
      "end": 1034.38,
      "text": "Mental model becomes super simple or at least much more simpler"
    },
    {
      "start": 1034.42,
      "end": 1037.94,
      "text": "than what it would have been in a big ball of mud"
    },
    {
      "start": 1037.94,
      "end": 1039.34,
      "text": "where everything talks to everything."
    },
    {
      "start": 1039.94,
      "end": 1042.22,
      "text": "Less risk when making updates."
    },
    {
      "start": 1042.84,
      "end": 1043.96,
      "text": "This is a big one."
    },
    {
      "start": 1044.38,
      "end": 1047.42,
      "text": "Systems need to remain flexible, ready for change."
    },
    {
      "start": 1048.4,
      "end": 1051.3,
      "text": "And if everything's depending on everything else,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1051.68,
      "end": 1058.08,
      "text": "change becomes risky and due to that high risk is often not done."
    },
    {
      "start": 1058.84,
      "end": 1060.94,
      "text": "Which means you get stuck in the mud."
    },
    {
      "start": 1061.46,
      "end": 1065.96,
      "text": "I used to travel with 4x4 in Africa."
    },
    {
      "start": 1066.6,
      "end": 1069.8,
      "text": "I've got amazing photos of where we got stuck in the mud"
    },
    {
      "start": 1069.8,
      "end": 1073.74,
      "text": "and interestingly enough, they call this system"
    },
    {
      "start": 1073.74,
      "end": 1076.3,
      "text": "that everything depends on everything a big ball of mud."
    },
    {
      "start": 1077.36,
      "end": 1079.94,
      "text": "I would just say, it just reminds me back in the day"
    },
    {
      "start": 1079.94,
      "end": 1082.06,
      "text": "where a vehicle would get stuck in the mud."
    },
    {
      "start": 1082.52,
      "end": 1086.5,
      "text": "And sometimes I have stories where we were stuck for two days"
    },
    {
      "start": 1086.5,
      "end": 1088.9,
      "text": "in the mud in a Land Cruiser."
    },
    {
      "start": 1089.44,
      "end": 1091.26,
      "text": "So that's what you don't want."
    },
    {
      "start": 1091.32,
      "end": 1092.52,
      "text": "You want to stay nimble."
    },
    {
      "start": 1092.52,
      "end": 1095.9,
      "text": "You want to have a Lamborghini or a Corvette"
    },
    {
      "start": 1095.9,
      "end": 1099.92,
      "text": "or name your car, Porsche."
    },
    {
      "start": 1100.54,
      "end": 1102.2,
      "text": "And you want to be able to always move,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1102.62,
      "end": 1103.92,
      "text": "move your application forward,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1104.44,
      "end": 1107.34,
      "text": "adapt to business needs without getting stuck."
    },
    {
      "start": 1108.36,
      "end": 1109.8,
      "text": "Biggest, biggest benefit."
    },
    {
      "start": 1111.4,
      "end": 1111.82,
      "text": "Key takeaways."
    },
    {
      "start": 1112.28,
      "end": 1114.28,
      "text": "Protect business logic from changing technology."
    },
    {
      "start": 1115.94,
      "end": 1117.66,
      "text": "Keep the important rules at the center."
    },
    {
      "start": 1118.4,
      "end": 1123.02,
      "text": "Build so the core stays clean and stable."
    },
    {
      "start": 1124.58,
      "end": 1128.68,
      "text": "I would say mental model needs to be added here."
    },
    {
      "start": 1129.28,
      "end": 1130.84,
      "text": "Keep the mental model simple."
    },
    {
      "start": 1132.08,
      "end": 1134.74,
      "text": "So somebody asked one of the great developers."
    },
    {
      "start": 1135.88,
      "end": 1137.96,
      "text": "I can't really remember who he was,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1138.0,
      "end": 1140.28,
      "text": "but he's quoted in this book, Clean Architecture."
    },
    {
      "start": 1140.82,
      "end": 1142.84,
      "text": "What is a clean architecture?"
    },
    {
      "start": 1143.02,
      "end": 1145.84,
      "text": "And he said it's code that can fit into your head."
    },
    {
      "start": 1146.44,
      "end": 1149.26,
      "text": "And what it means is it's code that's easy to understand."
    },
    {
      "start": 1150.32,
      "end": 1152.92,
      "text": "And obviously that doesn't have anything to do with a computer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1153.34,
      "end": 1155.02,
      "text": "the machine, the PC, the Mac."
    },
    {
      "start": 1155.56,
      "end": 1157.08,
      "text": "It doesn't need to understand the code."
    },
    {
      "start": 1157.34,
      "end": 1158.0,
      "text": "It runs the code."
    },
    {
      "start": 1158.54,
      "end": 1160.26,
      "text": "This is for us to understand."
    },
    {
      "start": 1160.52,
      "end": 1162.8,
      "text": "It's for us to stay involved, stay in control,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1162.82,
      "end": 1166.26,
      "text": "and easily be able to change things and keep things stable."
    },
    {
      "start": 1168.78,
      "end": 1170.62,
      "text": "And that's sort of the story."
    },
    {
      "start": 1171.34,
      "end": 1175.92,
      "text": "Go ahead, implement Quest 1, Episode 3."
    },
    {
      "start": 1176.5,
      "end": 1180.3,
      "text": "I will see you in the code through of this quest."
    },
    {
      "start": 1180.5,
      "end": 1183.16,
      "text": "By the way, I'm going to use Codex to code through it."
    },
    {
      "start": 1183.92,
      "end": 1185.3,
      "text": "I've already done it, actually."
    },
    {
      "start": 1185.42,
      "end": 1186.26,
      "text": "It was mind-blowing."
    },
    {
      "start": 1186.72,
      "end": 1189.36,
      "text": "I'm excited for you to see how I use Codex"
    },
    {
      "start": 1189.46,
      "end": 1190.62,
      "text": "to implement this quest."
    },
    {
      "start": 1190.66,
      "end": 1193.26,
      "text": "And I've got some interesting takeaways on that."
    },
    {
      "start": 1193.64,
      "end": 1194.54,
      "text": "See you in the next episode."
    },
    {
      "start": 1194.92,
      "end": 1195.04,
      "text": "Cheers."
    }
  ],
